   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to the number of signatures of enrolled voters needed on a\ndesignating petition for any town office to be filled by all the voters of\ncertain towns and the number of signatures required on a designating petition\nfor a village election; and to provide for the repeal of such provisions upon\nthe expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5256",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5256-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 37,
       "fullName": "Shelley Mayer",
       "imgName": "623_shelley_mayer.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1143,
       "sessionMemberId": 1824,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "MAYER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5256\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to the number of signatures of enrolled voters needed\non a designating petition for any town office to be filled by all the\nvoters of certain towns and the number of signatures required on a\ndesignating petition for a village election; and to provide for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAn Act in relation to the number of signatures of enrolled voters needed\non a designating petition for any town office to be filled by all the\nvoters of certain towns and the number of signatures required on a\ndesignating petition for a village election; and to provide for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill provides that notwithstanding election law section\n6-136(2): (a) the number of signatures of enrolled voters needed on a\ndesignating petition for any town office to be filled by all the voters\nof towns containing more than twenty-five thousand and not more than\none-hundred thousand inhabitants, according to the last preceding feder-\nal enumeration, shall be two times the number of election districts in\nsuch town or three hundred signatures, whichever is less; (b) the number\nof signatures of enrolled voters needed on a designating petition for\nany town office to be filled by all the voters of towns containing twen-\nty-five thousand inhabitants or less, according to the last preceding\nfederal enumeration, shall be two times the number of election districts\nin such town or one hundred fifty signatures, whichever is less.\n\nSection 2 provides that notwithstanding election law section 6-204(2)\nand election law section 15-108(3)(b), the number of signatures required\non a designating petition for a village election shall be one and one-\nhalf per centum of the number of enrolled voters of the party residing\nin the village.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe continued impacts of the COVID-19 virus has made it necessary to\nminimize in-person petitioning. Maximizing safe and fair elections is\ncritical to the continued functioning of our government and democracy.\n\nThis legislation will significantly reduce the number of signatures\nneeded on a petition for towns and village elections required to be\nfiled in 2021. This legislation will adapt our current election laws to\nensure that our democratic process can continue to operate during the\npandemic safely and securely.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed on December 31, 2021.\n",
